#36754
"By A Monument"
"This enclosure seems to have been visited numerous times judging by the
plethora of footprints on the ground and different markings on the rocky
wall.  The air is pleasantly cool here and filled with an invigorating
fragrance.  Capturing your attention at the northwestern corner stands a tall
obsidian statue in the shape of a human hand.  Dangling around its fingers
high above you are what appear to be some large horns.  The horns' reflective
gleam and shiny veneer make it difficult to judge how long they've been there.
"
"[Dalthas] how about adding get horn?
"
