"Within A Forest"
"A few tree stumps stand here, nearly buried in piles of decayed leaves that
circle their base.  Numerous rings can still be spotted at the core of each
stump.  Littering the hard, blackened soil are mulches the size of elephant
teeth.  A gust of tepid air arrives from the east, carrying with it a dry,
smoky smell.  To the south are birch trees with barks partially stained with a
black powdery substance.
"
