#36900
"Inside A Cavernous Passage"
"The passage through the cave has been carved off the carbonate wall to the
north and twists around to the south and east.  The walls resemble camel humps
as they rise above one another.  Dripping down one hump to the next is warm,
brackish water.  A thin layer of soot and dust carpets the rocky floor.
"
""
