#36901
"Inside A Cavernous Passage"
"A stalagmite has formed to the southeast.  It is thick as an aged oak tree and
reaches a few feet apart from the stalactite directly above it.  The dripping
from the stalactite is rare but steady.  Piles of soft dust have settled
beside the cave's walls to the south and east, where movement has been sealed
off by additional layers of molten rock.  The only visible path is through the
north and west.
"
